   "type": "Feature",
   "properties": {
    "candidate": "Proposed Bongo Beach administrative boundary - Candidate 1 (DRAFT)",
    "status": "DRAFT - not confirmed, not surveyed, not submitted to CPD",
    "north_control": "N-01, committee-pinned control point at 41.788158,-87.577448 (south side of the 59th Street Harbor pier). Boundary from N-01 south to the v4 tie point follows Jackson Park #19 official polygon (G1) exactly on both the lake/harbor side and the DuSable Drive side.",
    "south_control": "S-01, committee-pinned control point at 41.776037,-87.574900 (S. Coast Guard Drive bridge/neck by Jackson Park Outer Harbor). The west (road) side from S-01 north to the v4 tie point follows Jackson Park #19 official polygon (G1) exactly. The east side from the v4 tie point down to S-01 is a straight PLACEHOLDER segment, not traced geometry — whether the boundary should follow the Inner/Outer Harbor shoreline, the harbor water, or a simpler cut is still an open decision (see the water-boundary question in the boundary-control section).",
    "east_control": "Existing lakeward boundary of Jackson Park #19, extended north to N-01 using real Park #19 vertices; unresolved (placeholder) between the v4 tie and S-01",
    "west_control": "DuSable Lake Shore Drive / S. Coast Guard Drive alignment, extended to N-01 and to S-01 using real Park #19 vertices, which run very close to the road on both new stretches",
    "approx_acres": 42.33,
    "revision": "v5 - north extended to N-01 (59th St. Harbor pier) and south extended to S-01 (Outer Harbor neck), both using real Jackson Park #19 boundary data on the west/road side and (north only) the east/lake side; south-east (harbor) side between the old v4 tie and S-01 is an explicit straight placeholder pending the harbor water-inclusion decision"
   },
